   "output": "You are comparing two drafts written from the same brief. Read no other file, and do not run commands or browse; judge only the text below.\n\nBrief: Write the landing page copy for `sackview`, following the tool page section order.\n\n<<<DRAFT A\n# sackview: see inside a ZIP before you unpack it\n\nList archive entries and check their sizes before extracting elsewhere.\n\n```sh\npipx install sackview\n```\n\nZIP archives only \u00b7 Offline inspection\n\n## Archive inspection\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip\n```\n\nEach entry shows its name, compressed size, and unpacked size.\n\n## Commands\n\n### Find the largest entries\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --largest 10\n```\n\nShow the ten entries with the largest unpacked sizes, largest first.\n\n### Filter by name\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --find '*.csv'\n```\n\nShow only entries whose names match the pattern.\n\n## Keys\n\nNo key bindings are specified in the supplied reference.\n\n## Check disk space before extracting\n\nsackview displays the total unpacked size. Use it to check available disk space before extracting the archive elsewhere.\n\n## Good to know\n\n**Archive safety**  \nsackview never extracts entries or changes the archive.\n\n**Privacy**  \nNo archive contents are sent to a service.\n\n**Unsupported formats**  \nOther archive formats produce an unsupported-format message and return exit code 24.\nDRAFT A>>>\n\n<<<DRAFT B\n# See inside a ZIP before unpacking\n\nsackview shows what is inside a ZIP archive before you unpack it. Check the total unpacked size against available disk space before extracting elsewhere.\n\n```sh\npipx install sackview\n```\n\nInspection works offline and sends no archive contents to a service.\n\n## Inspect an archive\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip\n```\n\nEach entry shows its name, compressed size, and unpacked size.\n\n## Commands\n\nShow the ten entries with the largest unpacked sizes, largest first:\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --largest 10\n```\n\nShow only entries whose names match a pattern:\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --find '*.csv'\n```\n\n## Good to know\n\n### Archive safety\n\nsackview never extracts entries or changes the archive.\n\n### Supported formats\n\nsackview supports ZIP archives only. Other archive formats produce an unsupported-format message and return exit code 24.\nDRAFT B>>>\n\nAnswer each question with \"A\", \"B\", or \"SAME\":\n- \"reader\": Could a first-time reader do what they came to do?\n- \"careful\": Does it read like a careful person wrote it?\n- \"overall\": Which draft is better overall?\n\nReply with only JSON: {\"reader\": \"A\", \"careful\": \"A\", \"overall\": \"A\", \"reason\": \"<one sentence>\"}",
